            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "definition",
            "title": "Compilers",
            "text": "Compilers are translators that convert entire programs from high-level languages into machine code before execution. Their purpose is to optimize the code and convert it into efficient machine code."
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "GCC: the GNU Compiler Collection for C and C++.",
              "javac: the compiler for Java programs."
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
